r and didn't  know what was happening we were all  wrong the doors opened and attendees  swarmed the booth within five minutes  attendees realized they could just take  games and walk away a small group  grabbed armfuls of the free games and  left but most people that does suck but  most people paid something within an  hour the booth looked like this so one  hour  until it was completely gone we ran  under games in 51 minutes and made eight  thousand dollars and forty sorry eight  thousand and forty two dollars or 18.7  percent of the game's retail value in  other words we lost 685  per  minute and the booth cost 43 000  that's nuts um though i do want to know  if you weren't already a web that a lot  of companies do consider conventions to  be a  kind of a financial sink because of  things like shipping cost or freight or  whatever just to get all of the product  actually to the show floor and then set  up the booth so generally it is more  about marketing which is obviously what  they use this opportunity for or about  community engagement and a lot less  about making money uh tani's put lots of  other stuff in the payment box too  that's actually really cool i like that  the free pizza some things you put in  our po box five canadian dollars 10  euros 80 philippine pesos one chinese  yuan one cubone pokemon card xy  breakthrough  one magic the gathering eternal masters  booster pack rapper cool handwritten any  pizza free and twisted flicks plus kpc  coupon from papa murphy's and kirkland  wa that's actually awesome one one  dollar bill folded into a bow tie  one feeltheburn.org one dollar bill and  two halves of a one dollar bill  wow you stole a lot of games this is why  we can't have nice things so they  updated it once we sold out we figured  we had to figure out what to do with our  boot space on saturday we gave space to  artists who weren't able to get a table  at the con people showed up to exhibit  cosplay horns board games recycled  journals and comic art that is very cool  on the last day of the con we set up a  station for mailing letters to  representatives write a letter to the  government we provided pens paper  postage envelopes writing tips and the  address of every us senator and i guess  the idea was that you could write  whatever you wanted and they would be  mailed um over 200 letters were written  by conatoni's including the most badass  imperative imperator imperator imperator  furiosa cosplay we've ever seen  that's very cool again this is marketing  but there's bad marketing in the games  industry and there's this again i will  talk about that for spoken uh trailer  that blew up on twitter controversially  in my next q a because enough people  have asked me about it that i was like  this has to be in the q a there's so  many youtube comments people asking me  about it um but i just think you know  they they have done some very genuine  seeming marketing it's of course still  marketing it is still uh done to to get  people like me to talk about it  but they have just a history of doing  the stuff and again i don't believe they  have like a fully tidy history i think  the cards against humanity has done some  questionable things as an organization i  just don't know what those are i just  want to point that out because i'm not  trying to say like they're an incredible  company it's just i think that other  companies in the industry have things to  learn in terms of marketing and in terms  of like how to actually appeal to people  uh where it seems like such a struggle  in some cases if there's anything that  i've learned in my time working in  tripoli game development this is not to  speak in my own studio just now that i'm  in game dev rather than in game  journalism world the people that i've  always known in game never a lot more  honest with me than they used to be  because they're not hiding anything the  developers in the marketing teams do not  get on that relationship is like  if you felt negatively about something  to do with video game marketing my  perspective from friends who work in the  industry would be that the studios felt  negative long before you did  and then just seethed when the community  reaction was negative as well and the  devs were like we [ __ ] told you  marketing and the marketing team goes  and nobody gets upset with them just  putting that context out there so those  are my three stories this week it was  actually kind of like a light week on  games news and i suspect that that is  because gamescom is coming up i have  some cool stuff planned for gamescom i  have some uh games that i've already got  exclusive hands-on locked in for that i  will be able to post as soon as the  embargoes are up it might do some  interviews and definitely do some  reactions to some trailers so stay tuned  for that that is the week of my birthday  i think it actually starts on my  birthday august 24th um so that's  probably why there's not a lot of news  right now is that all the news is  logically just waiting for gamescom it  happens but thank you all for watching  this week's good news or news that i  feel positively about as i guess i  should title it more realistically i  hope you feel positive too my friends  and thank you again to scentbird for  sponsoring the video link is in the  description if you want to check them  out i use it i smell good it's great  i'll see you guys next time bye
 

